# Response headers for the hosted app on Cloudflare Pages (admin.invoicing.co),
# copied into the site by .github/workflows/web.yml (docs/web-deploy.md).
# Everything revalidates: only flutter_bootstrap.js's entrypoints carry a ?v=
# hash, and a stale engine or asset beside a new bootstrap breaks the boot.
# When Flutter 3.50's --web-content-hash names every file by its hash, give the
# hashed paths their own rule with `! Cache-Control` first (Pages adds the
# values of every matching rule) and `public, max-age=31536000, immutable`.
# Never a `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` (say, for skwasm threads):
# it cuts this page off from the Google, Microsoft and Apple sign-in windows,
# which then never report back. `same-origin-allow-popups` is the most it can
# be (test/lint/web_sign_in_popups_test.dart).
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
